linux-zako

Linux-libre with the Zen patchset and the BORE scheduler on top.

Base
    linux-libre 7.3.5 gnu tarball
    https://www.linux-libre.fsfla.org/pub/linux-libre/releases/7.3.5-gnu/
    sha256 00f30f9cc4328a4b0a8d8a71349f9dc9fabed762f0a27993160e319377ef5753
    the tarball and deblob scripts in that directory are signed by Alexandre Oliva

Build
    tar xf linux-libre-7.3.5-gnu.tar.xz
    cd linux-libre-7.3.5
    git apply ../patches/7.3/0001-zen-7.3.5-zen1.patch
    git apply ../patches/7.3/0002-sched-bore-7.0.0.patch
    make olddefconfig
    make LOCALVERSION=-zako1

    Enable CONFIG_SCHED_BORE in olddefconfig. Keep CONFIG_SCHED_ALT (BMQ, PDS)
    off, it costs cgroup v2 cpu.weight and cpu.max, sched_ext and SCHED_CORE.

Patches
    Applied in the order listed in series/7.3. 0001 is the Zen patchset, 0002 is
    BORE rebased onto it.

Tags
    v7.3.5-zako1 is linux-libre 7.3.5 with revision 1 of this queue. Tags do not
    move once published.

Next version
    The queue moves when Linux-libre, Zen and BORE have all reached it.
